><name><surname>Fakan</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Puvion</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The ultrastructural visualization of nuclear and extranucleolar RNA synthesis and distribution</article-title><source>Int. Rev. Cytol.</source><volume>65</volume><year>1980</year><fpage>255</fpage><lpage>299</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6156137</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="JacksonandCook1985"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jackson</surname><given-names>D.A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Cook</surname><given-names>P.R.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Transcription occurs at a nucleoskeleton</article-title><source>EMBO (Eur. Mol. Biol. Organ.) J.</source><volume>4</volume><year>1985</year><fpage>919</fpage><lpage>925</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="Johnsonetal2000"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>C.V.</given-names></name><name><surname>Primorac</surname><given-names>D.</given-names></name><name><surname>McKinstry</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>McNeil</surname><given-names>J.A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Rowe</surname><given-names>D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Lawrence</surname><given-names>J.B.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tracking COLA1A1 RNA in osteogenesis imperfectasplice-defective transcripts initiate transport from the gene but are retained within the SC-35 domain</article-title><source>J. Cell Biol.</source><volume>In press</volume><year>2000</year></citation></ref><ref id="Kruhlaketal2000"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kruhlak</surname><given-names>M.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Lever</surname><given-names>M.A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Fischle</surname><given-names>W.</given-name